== 2. Where those 14 pixels are ==
Re-ran scripts/lib/png-diff.mjs on the two pairs to get the worst-box geometry the
probe only prints on failure, then cropped both captures at that box and looked:

  12-editor-workspace 1280x800: 5/1017850 px, worst box 62x3 at 276,170
  14-conflict-dialog  1280x800: 9/1017775 px, worst box 345x3 at 276,207

Both boxes are 3 px tall and sit inside the editor's tool rail (select, pan, text,
image, shape, draw, duplicate). Every icon is present, the same size, at the same
x — the residual is anti-aliasing along SVG strokes. The geometry rules out the
alternative reading: a moved or resized element produces a diff box the height of
that element, not a 3-pixel band. Neither box is adjacent to a mask rect, so it is
not mask-edge bleed either.

