107 captures are compared with no mask at all. The masked content is exactly what
differs legitimately between two runs: the throwaway account's identity, relative
timestamps, and a transient live-region whose text depends on when the screenshot
lands. `time` binding 0 rects is worth stating rather than assuming — a mask that
matches nothing hides nothing, and nobody should later "fix" its absence.

